Fix SIGSEGV in the Base "Create Database" wizard when Firebird is not built.

OGeneralPageWizard::getDatasourceName() hardcodes the Firebird driver as the
default selection of the data source type list:

    return m_pCollection->getTypeDisplayName( u"sdbc:firebird:"_ustr );

openSUSE Tumbleweed has no firebird package any more (boo#1179203 - the
package was dropped from Factory), so we build with --disable-firebird-sdbc
and there is no "sdbc:firebird:" entry in the driver registry.
getTypeDisplayName() returns an empty string, set_active_text("") matches
nothing, and the combo box is left with no selection at all.

Picking "Connect to an existing database" and pressing Next then runs into
OGeneralPageWizard::FillItemSet(), which indexes m_aURLPrefixes with the
unchecked result of get_active() - that is, with -1:

    #0  rtl_uString_acquire (pThis=0x91) at sal/rtl/ustring.cxx:1114
    #1  rtl::OUString::OUString at include/rtl/ustring.hxx:210
    #2  dbaui::OGeneralPageWizard::FillItemSet at dbaccess/source/ui/dlg/generalpage.cxx:599
    #3  dbaui::OGenericAdministrationPage::DeactivatePage at dbaccess/source/ui/dlg/adminpages.cxx:66
    #5  dbaui::ODbTypeWizDialogSetup::leaveState at dbaccess/source/ui/dlg/dbwizsetup.cxx:647
    #6  vcl::WizardMachine::ShowPage(short)

Fall back to the first available type when the preferred default is not part
of the build, and bounds-check nEntry in both FillItemSet() implementations,
the same way OnDatasourceTypeSelected() already does.

Index: dbaccess/source/ui/dlg/generalpage.cxx
===================================================================
--- a/dbaccess/source/ui/dlg/generalpage.cxx
+++ b/dbaccess/source/ui/dlg/generalpage.cxx
@@ -211,6 +211,16 @@
 
         m_xDatasourceType->set_active_text(getDatasourceName(_rSet));
 
+        // The preferred default type is not necessarily part of every build:
+        // openSUSE Tumbleweed has no firebird package (boo#1179203), so
+        // LibreOffice is built with --disable-firebird-sdbc and the Firebird
+        // entry that OGeneralPageWizard::getDatasourceName() asks for simply
+        // does not exist.  set_active_text() then leaves the list box without
+        // any selection at all, and FillItemSet() goes on to index
+        // m_aURLPrefixes with -1.  Fall back to the first available type.
+        if (m_xDatasourceType->get_active() == -1 && m_xDatasourceType->get_count() > 0)
+            m_xDatasourceType->set_active(0);
+
         // notify our listener that our type selection has changed (if so)
         // FIXME: how to detect that it did not changed? (fdo#62937)
         setParentTitle( m_eCurrentSelection );
@@ -430,6 +440,11 @@
         bool bChangedSomething = false;
 
         const sal_Int32 nEntry = m_xDatasourceType->get_active();
+        if (nEntry == -1 || o3tl::make_unsigned(nEntry) >= m_aURLPrefixes.size())
+        {
+            SAL_WARN("dbaccess.ui.generalpage", "OGeneralPageDialog::FillItemSet: no data source type selected, nothing to commit");
+            return bChangedSomething;
+        }
         OUString sURLPrefix = m_aURLPrefixes[ nEntry ];
 
         if (m_xDatasourceType->get_value_changed_from_saved())
@@ -596,6 +611,11 @@
